# Every exported method of whatsmeow's Client that the sidecar does not call on purpose, with the reason (ADR 0048).
# tools/parity-report reads this file: a method the sidecar's code does not reach and this file does not list is
# missing, as a method a whatsmeow bump adds is. One method per line, `Name: reason`; grouped by whatsmeow file.
# A follow-up issue as the reason means the method is in scope and not built yet; "out of v1 scope (#36)" is a scope
# decision made with the report, in #36.

# appstate.go
MarkNotDirty: clearing an app state dirty bit is out of v1 scope (#36); chat state recovery fetches the app state instead (ADR 0031), and whatsmeow's own call is commented out (connectionevents.go:95)

# broadcast.go
GetStatusPrivacy: statuses are a §1 non-goal

# business.go
GetOrderDetails: business features are a §1 non-goal

# call.go
RejectCall: calls are a §1 non-goal

# client.go
AddEventHandler: the sidecar's handlers use AddEventHandlerWithSuccessStatus, whose false return withholds the answer to a gated stanza (§13 invariant 2)
Connect: the sidecar connects with ConnectContext and its own lifetime context (ADR 0020, client.go:543-601)
IsLoggedIn: a session's state comes from whatsmeow's events and the store (§7.4)
RemoveEventHandler: the sidecar adds its handlers once per client and never removes them
RemoveEventHandlers: the sidecar adds its handlers once per client and never removes them
SetMaxParallelRetryReceiptHandling: whatsmeow's default (unlimited) is kept; no option, out of v1 scope (#36)
SetMediaHTTPClient: whatsmeow's HTTP clients are not configurable, out of v1 scope (#36)
SetPreLoginHTTPClient: whatsmeow's HTTP clients are not configurable, out of v1 scope (#36)
SetProxy: a proxy is not configurable, out of v1 scope (#36)
SetProxyAddress: a proxy is not configurable, out of v1 scope (#36)
SetSOCKSProxy: a proxy is not configurable, out of v1 scope (#36)
SetWebsocketHTTPClient: whatsmeow's HTTP clients are not configurable, out of v1 scope (#36)
StoreLIDPNMapping: whatsmeow stores the mappings it learns itself (message.go:52-54, notification.go:126, pair.go:231); the application only reads them (ADR 0028)
WaitForConnection: a session's state comes from whatsmeow's events (§7.4)

# connectionevents.go
SetPassive: whatsmeow sets passive false itself after it connects (connectionevents.go:200)

# download-to-file.go
DownloadFBToFile: Messenger and Instagram (FB) messages are not WhatsApp
DownloadMediaWithOnlyPathToFile: a MediaRef carries the keys and hashes, so DownloadMedia downloads and checks with DownloadMediaWithPathToFile (§7.6)
DownloadToFile: a MediaRef replaces the message as what DownloadMedia takes; it uses DownloadMediaWithPathToFile (§7.6)

# download.go
Download: DownloadMedia decrypts to the sidecar's own file and checks it whole before any plaintext leaves (§7.6), with DownloadMediaWithPathToFile; this one returns the plaintext in memory
DownloadAny: deprecated upstream (download.go)
DownloadFB: Messenger and Instagram (FB) messages are not WhatsApp
DownloadMediaWithOnlyPath: it takes no media key or hashes (download.go:248-250), which a MediaRef carries; DownloadMedia decrypts to the sidecar's own file and checks it (§7.6)
DownloadMediaWithPath: DownloadMedia decrypts to the sidecar's own file (§7.6), with DownloadMediaWithPathToFile; this one returns the plaintext in memory
DownloadThumbnail: a thumbnail's own download is out of v1 scope (#36); the message's inline thumbnail is in its content and Raw
FetchStickerPack: sticker packs are out of v1 scope (#36)

# group.go
GetGroupInfoFromInvite: invite messages are not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)
GetGroupRequestParticipants: join-request approval is not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)
GetLinkedGroupsParticipants: communities are not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)
GetSubGroups: communities are not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)
JoinGroupWithInvite: invite messages are not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)
LinkGroup: communities are not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)
SetGroupDescription: deprecated upstream as a duplicate of SetGroupTopic (group.go:1099), which SetGroupTopic covers
SetGroupJoinApprovalMode: join-request approval is not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)
SetGroupPhoto: group photos are not in the groups slice (ADR 0030); only the live tests' control calls it, in a livetest build (ADR 0060)
UnlinkGroup: communities are not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)
UpdateGroupRequestParticipants: join-request approval is not in the groups slice (ADR 0030)

# internals.go
DangerousInternals: whatsmeow's unexported internals are never called

# message.go
SendHistorySyncServerErrorReceipt: history sync reports a blob that cannot be downloaded (EXPIRED, INVALID, UNAVAILABLE) and never asks the phone to upload it again (ADR 0035)
SendProtocolMessageReceipt: whatsmeow sends the history sync and peer message receipts itself (message.go:910, 938)

# msgsecret.go
DecryptComment: encrypted comments are out of v1 scope (#36); one arrives with its content in Raw
DecryptReaction: encrypted reactions are out of v1 scope (#36); one arrives with its content in Raw
DecryptSecretEncryptedMessage: secret-encrypted edits (of events, polls and messages) are out of v1 scope (#36); one arrives with its content in Raw
EncryptComment: encrypted comments are out of v1 scope (#36)
EncryptPollVote: BuildPollVote calls it (msgsecret.go:392), which SendPollVote covers
EncryptReaction: encrypted reactions are out of v1 scope (#36)

# newsletter.go
AcceptTOSNotice: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
CreateNewsletter: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
FollowNewsletter: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
GetNewsletterInfo: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
GetNewsletterInfoWithInvite: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
GetNewsletterMessageUpdates: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
GetNewsletterMessages: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
GetSubscribedNewsletters: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
NewsletterMarkViewed: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
NewsletterSendReaction: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
NewsletterSubscribeLiveUpdates: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
NewsletterToggleMute: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
UnfollowNewsletter: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal

# pair-passkey.go
SendPasskeyConfirmation: pairing is by QR code or phone code (ADR 0021); passkey pairing is out of v1 scope (#36)
SendPasskeyResponse: pairing is by QR code or phone code (ADR 0021); passkey pairing is out of v1 scope (#36)

# privacysettings.go
GetPrivacySettings: the account's privacy settings are out of v1 scope (#36)
SetDefaultDisappearingTimer: the account's default disappearing timer is an account setting, out of v1 scope (#36)
SetPrivacySetting: the account's privacy settings are out of v1 scope (#36)
TryFetchPrivacySettings: the account's privacy settings are out of v1 scope (#36)

# push.go
GetServerPushNotificationConfig: push notifications are for a mobile app, not a companion device
RegisterForPushNotifications: push notifications are for a mobile app, not a companion device

# receipt.go
SetForceActiveDeliveryReceipts: delivery receipts follow the presence the application sets with SendPresence, as whatsmeow does by default (receipt.go:243-254, ADR 0027)

# send.go
BuildMessageKey: BuildRevoke and BuildReaction call it (send.go:540, 554), which SendRevoke and SendReaction cover; BuildEdit builds its key itself (send.go:616-633)
BuildUnavailableMessageRequest: whatsmeow requests an undecryptable message from the phone itself with AutomaticMessageRerequestFromPhone (retry.go:455, §7.2)
GenerateMessageID: the caller makes message ids, in the same format, so a repeat is idempotent (ADR 0025)
RevokeMessage: deprecated upstream in favour of BuildRevoke (send.go:504), which SendRevoke covers
SendPeerMessage: RequestHistory sends its peer message with SendMessage and Peer, as SendPeerMessage does (send.go:491-497), to pass an id of its own (history.go); whatsmeow sends its other peer messages itself (appstate.go:541, retry.go:455)

# sendfb.go
SendFBMessage: Messenger and Instagram (FB) messages are not WhatsApp

# upload.go
Upload: UploadMedia streams a path or chunks into UploadReader, which encrypts into the sidecar's temporary file (§7.6); this one takes the whole plaintext in memory
UploadNewsletter: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal
UploadNewsletterReader: newsletters (channels) are a §1 non-goal

# user.go
GetBotListV2: bots are out of v1 scope (#36)
GetBotProfiles: bots are out of v1 scope (#36)
GetBusinessProfile: business features are a §1 non-goal
GetContactQRLink: contact QR links are out of v1 scope (#36)
GetUserDevices: whatsmeow looks up the devices it sends to itself (send.go:1198); the application addresses users, not devices
GetUserDevicesContext: whatsmeow looks up the devices it sends to itself (send.go:1198); the application addresses users, not devices
ResolveBusinessMessageLink: business features are a §1 non-goal
ResolveContactQRLink: contact QR links are out of v1 scope (#36)
SetStatusMessage: the account's about text is out of v1 scope (#36)
